messages:  ["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nA committee works for two years and is composed of 4 members each year, 2 of which are from the following 4 judges: F, G, H and I, and the other 2 members are from the following 3 scientists: V, Y and Z. Each year, the committee is chaired by one member. A member who chairs the first year must retire from the committee during the second year. The person who chairs the second year must be a member of the committee during the first year. The committee members must meet the following conditions: G and V cannot be members of the committee in the same year. H and Y cannot be members of this committee in the same year. Each year, only one of I and V is a member of this committee.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if H is the chairman in the first year, which of the followings can be the chairman in the second year?\n# Options:\nA) F\nB) G\nC) Y\nD) II think the correct option is: D\n\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the given information and constraints step by step:\n\n1. **Committee Composition:**\n   - 4 members each year: 2 judges (F, G, H, I) and 2 scientists (V, Y, Z).\n   - 2 judges and 2 scientists each year.\n   - Each year, the committee is chaired by one member.\n\n2. **Chairman Conditions:**\n   - A member who chairs the first year must retire from the committee during the second year.\n   - The person who chairs the second year must be a member of the committee during the first year.\n   - G and V cannot be members of the committee in the same year.\n   - H and Y cannot be members of the committee in the same year.\n   - Only one of I and V is a member of the committee each year.\n\n3. **Given Information:**\n   - H is the chairman in the first year.\n   - H and Y cannot be members of the committee in the same year.\n   - G and V cannot be members of the committee in the same year.\n   - Only one of I and V is a member of the committee each year.\n\n4. **First Year:**\n   - H is the chairman.\n   - H and Y cannot be members of the committee.\n   - G and V cannot be members of the committee.\n   - Only one of I and V is a member of the committee.\n\n5. **Second Year:**\n   - The person who chairs the second year must be a member of the committee during the first year.\n   - H is the chairman in the first year, so H cannot be a member of the committee in the second year.\n   - G and V cannot be members of the committee in the same year, so G cannot be a member of the committee in the second year.\n   - Only one of I and V is a member of the committee each year, so V cannot be a member of the committee in the second year.\n   - Therefore, I must be the only member of the committee in the second year.\n\n6. **Possible Members for Second Year:**\n   - The only member of the committee in the second year is I.\n   - The only person who can be the chairman in the second year is I.\n\n7. **Conclusion:**\n   - The only possible chairman for the second year is I.\nThe correct option is:"]
