messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe amount of time it takes for most of a worker\'s occupational knowledge and skills to become obsolete has been declining because of the introduction of advanced manufacturing technology (AMT). Given the rate at which AMT is currently being introduced in manufacturing, the average worker\'s old skills become obsolete and new skills are required within as little as five years.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following plans, if feasible, would allow a company to prepare most effectively for the rapid obsolescence of skills described above?\n# Options:\nA) The company will ensure that it can offer its employees any training necessary for meeting their job requirements.\nB) The company will develop a program to offer selected employees the opportunity to receive training six years after they were originally hired.\nC) The company will increase its investment in amt every year for a period of at least five years.\nD) The company will periodically survey its employees to determine how the introduction of amt has affected them.I think the correct option is: B\n\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and the question step by step:\n1. The context states that the amount of time it takes for a worker\'s occupational knowledge and skills to become obsolete is decreasing due to the introduction of advanced manufacturing technology (AMT).\n2. It specifically mentions that new skills are required within as little as five years for most workers.\n3. The question asks which plan would allow a company to prepare most effectively for this rapid obsolescence of skills.\n4. We need to evaluate each option to determine which one aligns best with the given information.\nOption A: "The company will ensure that it can offer its employees any training necessary for meeting their job requirements."\n- This option directly addresses the need for training to keep up with the rapid obsolescence of skills.\n- It implies that the company will provide the necessary resources and support for employees to acquire new skills.\n- This aligns well with the context, as it directly counters the problem of skills becoming obsolete.\nOption B: "The company will develop a program to offer selected employees the opportunity to receive training six years after they were originally hired."\n- This option suggests a delayed approach to training, which is not aligned with the context.\n- The context indicates that skills become obsolete within five years, so offering training six years later would be too late.\n- This option does not effectively prepare for the rapid obsolescence of skills.\nOption C: "The company will increase its investment in AMT every year for a period of at least five years."\n- While this option is related to AMT, it focuses on the company\'s investment in AMT rather than preparing employees for the obsolescence of their skills.\n- Increasing investment in AMT does not directly address the need for employees to acquire new skills.\n- This option does not effectively prepare for the rapid obsolescence of skills.\nOption D: "The company will periodically survey its employees to determine how the introduction of AMT has affected them."\n- This option suggests gathering information about the impact of AMT on employees.\n- While this could be useful for understanding the situation, it does not directly address the need for employees to acquire new skills.\n- This option does not effectively prepare for the rapid obsolescence of skills.\nAfter evaluating all the options, the most effective plan to prepare for the rapid obsolescence of skills described in the context is Option A.\n</think>\n<answer>\nA\n</answer>\nThe correct option is:']
