      "index": 0,
      "text": "D\n\n2. **Analyzing Each Option**:\n   - **Option A**: \"In order to better sell steel, the owner of the steel plant gave a gift of one million to the contractor in the neighboring county.\"\n     - This option involves a gift given to a contractor, which is not a commercial activity. It is a form of bribery or political influence rather than promoting a product or service.\n   - **Option B**: \"In order to become president, Obama did not hesitate to make a speech on TV and newspapers.\"\n     - This option involves a political campaign, not a commercial activity. The purpose is to gain political power, not to promote a product or service.\n   - **Option C**: \"The company stipulates that office computers must use a unified brand.\"\n     - This option involves a company policy for office computers, which is a business decision rather than a commercial promotion. It does not involve the company bearing the cost to promote a specific product or service.\n   - **Option D**: \"Li Ning brand clothing sponsored the French sports delegation to go to the Olympic games, and obtained good social and economic benefits.\"\n     - This option involves a company (Li Ning) sponsoring an event (Olympic games) to promote its brand. The company bears the cost of the sponsorship and the promotion is through a medium (Olympic games). This fits the definition of advertising perfectly.\n\n3. **Conclusion**:\n   - Based on the definition of advertising and the analysis of each option, the correct option is D.\n</think>\n<answer>\nD\n</answer>",
