      "text": "D) Developing countries began industrialization and modernization in an external environment completely different from developed countries\n\nLet's evaluate each option:\nA) The per capita gnp of less than us $300 is a sign of developing countries\n- This statement is not directly supported by the context. The context only mentions the range from $300 to $4,000 as a period of social shock, but it does not define the lower limit as a sign of developing countries.\nB) The per capita gnp of more than 4000 us dollars is a sign of developed countries\n- This statement is not supported by the context. The context does not provide a specific upper limit for developed countries' GNP.\nC) Many developing countries have experienced violent social shocks in the process of their modernization\n- This statement is partially supported by the context. The context mentions that a period of $300 to $4,000 is a period of social shock, but it does not explicitly state that many developing countries have experienced violent social shocks.\nD) Developing countries began industrialization and modernization in an external environment completely different from developed countries\n- This statement is directly supported by the context. The context mentions that even developed countries have experienced similar periods of social shock during their modernization process, implying that the external environment for developing countries' modernization might be different from that of developed countries.\nTherefore, the correct option is D.\n</think>\n<answer>\nD\n</answer>",
