iterati artists lags behind their creative level.\n- The context does not provide any information about the appreciation level of literati artists compared to their creative level. It only mentions their dominance in the discussion and the need for a more objective evaluation. This statement cannot be directly inferred from the given context.\n\nB) In ancient times, many talented literati and artists were buried because of prejudice.\n- The context does not mention any specific instances of talented literati and artists being "buried" due to prejudice. It only discusses the need for a more objective evaluation of non-literati artists. This statement is not supported by the provided information.\n\nC) The literati have been in a strong position in the field of Chinese painting theory for a long time.\n- The context explicitly states that "Chinese literati have dominated the discussion space of painting for a long time." This statement is directly supported by the given information.\n\nD) The difference of interest between ancient literati painting and non-literati painting has a long history.\n- While the context mentions the need for a more objective evaluation of non-literati artists, it does not provide information about the historical difference in interest between literati and non-literati painting. This statement is not directly supported by the provided information.\nThe correct option is:']
