messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nMotivation is the reason why people act, it can arouse action, so that the activity points to a certain goal.Depending on the source of the motive, it can be divided into internal motivation and extrinsic motive. Intrinsic motivation refers to the purpose of behavior to experience the joy and satisfaction brought about by the corresponding activities.Extrinsic motivation refers to the purpose of the act in order to obtain other external results or avoid punishment.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following options is most likely to reflect the underlying motivation?\n# Options:\nA) In order to keep fit, xiao zhao insists on exercising\nB) Mr. zhang loves his profession very much and enjoys the process of teaching and educating people\nC) Xiaofang took the first place in the swimming competition, and she was proud of herself.\nD) In order not to let parents disappointed, xiaoming very hard to study, and strive to enter the ideal schoolI think the correct option is: D\n\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and the question step by step:\n1. The context provides definitions for motivation:\n   - Motivation is the reason why people act.\n   - It can be internal or extrinsic.\n   - Intrinsic motivation is about experiencing joy and satisfaction from the activity itself.\n   - Extrinsic motivation is about obtaining external results or avoiding punishment.\n2. The question asks us to identify which option most likely reflects the underlying motivation based on these definitions.\n3. Let\'s analyze each option:\n   A) "In order to keep fit, Xiao Zhao insists on exercising"\n      - This option shows extrinsic motivation. Xiao Zhao is exercising to achieve a specific goal (keeping fit), not for the joy or satisfaction of the activity itself.\n   B) "Mr. Zhang loves his profession very much and enjoys the process of teaching and educating people"\n      - This option clearly shows intrinsic motivation. Mr. Zhang enjoys the process of teaching and educating people, which is the joy and satisfaction he gets from the activity itself.\n   C) "Xiaofang took the first place in the swimming competition, and she was proud of herself."\n      - This option also shows extrinsic motivation. Xiaofang is proud of herself for winning the competition, which is an external result she wants to achieve.\n   D) "In order not to let parents disappointed, Xiaoming very hard to study, and strive to enter the ideal school"\n      - This option demonstrates extrinsic motivation as well. Xiaoming is studying to avoid parental disappointment, which is an external result he wants to achieve.\n4. Based on the definitions provided, the option that most clearly reflects intrinsic motivation is B.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB</answer>\nThe correct option is:']
