      "text": "C\n\nReasoning for Option C:\n- The context uses the analogy of a supermarket needing different numbers of security guards based on its size.\n- It concludes that if a supermarket uses three security guards, it must be a big supermarket.\n- This reasoning is similar to the context's reasoning about herbal antibiotics being more effective due to their complexity (many active ingredients) compared to standard antibiotics (one active ingredient).\n- Option C uses an analogy to draw a conclusion about the size of a supermarket based on the number of security guards it employs.\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.\n</answer>",
