messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nOf the various food containers made of recycled Styrofoam, egg cartons are among the easiest to make. Because egg shells keep the actual food to be consumed from touching the Styrofoam, used Styrofoam need not be as thoroughly cleaned when made into egg cartons as when made into other food containers.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which one of the following is most strongly supported by the information above?\n# Options:\nA) Not every type of food container made of recycled styrofoam is effectively prevented from coming into contact with the food it contains.\nB) The main reason styrofoam must be thoroughly cleaned when recycled is to remove any residual food that has come into contact with the styrofoam.\nC) No food containers other than egg cartons can safely be made of recycled styrofoam that has not been thoroughly cleaned.\nD) There are some foods that cannot be packaged in recycled styrofoam no matter how the styrofoam is recycled.I think the correct option is: B\n\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and analyze each option step by step.\n\n1. **Context Analysis:**\n   - Egg cartons are among the easiest to make from recycled Styrofoam.\n   - Egg shells keep the food from touching the Styrofoam, so used Styrofoam doesn\'t need to be as thoroughly cleaned when made into egg cartons as when made into other food containers.\n\n2. **Option A:**\n   - "Not every type of food container made of recycled styrofoam is effectively prevented from coming into contact with the food it contains."\n   - This statement is not directly supported by the context. The context only mentions that egg cartons are an exception, not that all food containers are not effectively prevented from coming into contact with the food.\n\n3. **Option B:**\n   - "The main reason styrofoam must be thoroughly cleaned when recycled is to remove any residual food that has come into contact with the styrofoam."\n   - This statement is not supported by the context. The context does not mention the main reason for thorough cleaning; it only states that egg cartons don\'t need thorough cleaning.\n\n4. **Option C:**\n   - "No food containers other than egg cartons can safely be made of recycled styrofoam that has not been thoroughly cleaned."\n   - This statement is not supported by the context. The context only mentions that egg cartons don\'t need thorough cleaning, but it does not imply that other containers cannot be made from uncleaned Styrofoam.\n\n5. **Option D:**\n   - "There are some foods that cannot be packaged in recycled styrofoam no matter how the styrofoam is recycled."\n   - This statement is not directly supported by the context. The context does not mention any limitations on the types of foods that can be packaged in recycled Styrofoam.\nThe correct option is:']
