messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization has designated 2008 as the year of the Potato. The potato, also known as Tudou, is called a hidden treasure by United Nations experts. The United Nations named a year after a crop, which appeared only once in history, that is 2003, the International year of Rice. Why is it that this year\'s protagonist is not Corn, Apple, but the potato, which is buried deep in the ground and inconspicuous? Because potatoes are needed to solve the problem of global food security.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is the most accurate summary of this passage?\n# Options:\nA) Potatoes and rice are both important crops.\nB) Attention should be paid to the issue of global food security.\nC) Tudou is raised to the strategic height of food security.\nD) The potential great value of potatoes needs to be further developed.I think the correct option is: A\n\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and question step by step and analyze each option carefully.\n</think>\n<answer>\nFirst, let\'s understand the context:\n- The United Nations has designated 2008 as the Year of the Potato.\n- The potato is called a "hidden treasure" by United Nations experts.\n- This is the first time a crop has been named after a year.\n- The International Year of Rice was in 2003.\n- The reason for naming the year after the potato is to address global food security.\nThe correct option is:']
