messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAnalogical argument is based on the sameness or similarity of two objects in some attributes, and infers that the two objects are also the same or similar in other attributes. Its logical form is that object A has the attributes of a, b, c and d. Object B has properties of a, b, c. So object B has the property of d.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the followings belongs to analogical argument?\n# Options:\nA) Tao yuanming does not bow for five buckets of rice, li bai does not destroy eyebrows and bend over power. this shows that ambitious people are not proud of high officials and generous salaries\nB) Both light and sound have the phenomena of linear propagation, refraction and reflection, so light, like sound, also has fluctuation\nC) Compared with some people who are irresponsible in their work and afraid of heavy work, comrade bethune is extremely responsible for his work and extremely enthusiastic towards his comrades and the people, which shows that comrade bethune has a great spirit of being unselfish and dedicated to others\nD) Silver and copper are both metals with electrical conductivity, but the resistivity of silver is lower, so silver is more suitable to be a conductive material than copperI think the correct option is: D\n\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify which option fits the definition of an analogical argument. According to the definition provided, an analogical argument compares two objects based on their similarities in certain attributes and then infers that they are similar in other attributes as well. Let\'s analyze each option step by step:\n\nA) "Tao Yuanming does not bow for five buckets of rice, Li Bai does not destroy eyebrows and bend over power. This shows that ambitious people are not proud of high officials and generous salaries."\n- This option does not fit the definition of an analogical argument. It is making a generalization about ambitious people based on specific examples, rather than comparing two objects based on similarities in attributes.\n\nB) "Both light and sound have the phenomena of linear propagation, refraction, and reflection, so light, like sound, also has fluctuation."\n- This option fits the definition of an analogical argument. It compares light and sound based on their similarities in linear propagation, refraction, and reflection, and then infers that they share the property of fluctuation. This is a clear example of an analogical argument.\n\nC) "Compared with some people who are irresponsible in their work and afraid of heavy work, Comrade Bethune is extremely responsible for his work and extremely enthusiastic towards his comrades and the people, which shows that Comrade Bethune has a great spirit of being unselfish and dedicated to others."\n- This option does not fit the definition of an analogical argument. It is making a comparison between two individuals based on their attributes and then concluding that one has a specific quality. This is more of a comparative argument rather than an analogical one.\n\nD) "Silver and copper are both metals with electrical conductivity, but the resistivity of silver is lower, so silver is more suitable to be a conductive material than copper."\n- This option does not fit the definition of an analogical argument. It is making a comparison based on a specific attribute (electrical conductivity) and then concluding which material is more suitable based on another attribute (resistivity). This is more of a comparative argument.\nThe correct option is:']
