he concern about the future of live-action performances being replaced by computer-generated images and animations.\n\nB) The shooting of any film depends on the choice of the producer, and the actors can keep up with the development of the times.\n- This option implies that producers will continue to value live-action performances, and actors can adapt to new technologies. This directly addresses the actor's concern by suggesting that live-action performances will remain a priority, even as technology advances.\n\nC) The current high box office of 3d movies is only the result of people's temporary novelty, and the future is still unknown.\n- This option casts doubt on the long-term viability of 3D movies, but it doesn't directly address the actor's concern about live-action performances being replaced. It focuses more on the current popularity of 3D movies rather than the future of live-action performances.\n\nD) The film story can only be expressed by the heart and emotion of the actor, and its form of expression has nothing to do with the preferences of the director.\n- This option emphasizes the importance of the actor's performance and emotional expression, but it doesn't directly address the actor's concern about the future of live-action performances being replaced by computer-generated images and animations.\nThe correct option is:"]
