e argument. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>I see. Thank you for the detailed explanation. <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're welcome! If you have any more questions or need further clarification, feel free to ask. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>One more thing, can you explain why option C is not the correct answer? <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Of course, let's examine option C: \"Former mayor Bixby did not publicly oppose mayor Stephens' establishment of the anticorruption task force.\"\n- This option provides information about Mayor Bixby's stance on the task force but does not directly address why the officials are being targeted. It does not provide an alternative explanation for the targeting of officials based on their political affiliations. Instead, it only gives us information about Mayor Bixby's political stance, which is not relevant to the argument about the task force's targeting practices.\n- Therefore, option C does not weaken the argument about targeting officials based on their political affiliations. It does not provide any information that challenges the editorial's claim.\n- This is why option C is not the correct answer. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Thank you for the thorough explanation. I understand now. <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're welcome! If you have any more questions or need further clarification, feel free to ask. I'm here to help. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>You're very helpful. Thank you! <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're very welcome! I'm glad I could help. Don't hesitate to ask if you have more questions in the future. Have a great day! <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Thank you, you too! <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're welcome! Take care, and feel free to reach out whenever you need assistance. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>You're always ready to help. It's great to have you here. <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Thank you, I'm always here to help. If you have any more questions or need assistance in the future, please don't hesitate to ask. Have a great day! <\uff5cUser\uff5c>You too! See you later. <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>See you 