      "index": 0,
      "text": "D\n\nLet's analyze each option to determine which one does not fit the broken window effect:\n\nA) If the graffiti on a wall is not cleaned, the wall will soon be full of messy and ugly things.\n- This option describes a situation where one small problem (graffiti) leads to more problems (more graffiti). This aligns with the broken window effect.\n\nB) If a tributary is polluted and not treated, it may pollute the water quality of the whole basin.\n- This option describes a situation where one small problem (pollution in a tributary) can lead to a larger problem (pollution in the entire basin). This also aligns with the broken window effect.\n\nC) Once there is rubbish in a very clean place, people will throw their rubbish away without hesitation and will not feel ashamed.\n- This option describes a situation where one small problem (rubbish) can lead to more problems (people throwing more rubbish). This aligns with the broken window effect.\n\nD) If a few people in a group speak uncivilized languages and are not stopped, many people will soon speak uncivilized languages.\n- This option describes a situation where one small problem (a few people speaking uncivilized languages) can lead to more problems (many people speaking uncivilized languages). This aligns with the broken window effect.\n\nOption A, B, and C all describe scenarios where one small problem leads to more problems, which fits the broken window effect. However, option D describes a situation where one small problem (a few people speaking uncivilized languages) does not necessarily lead to more problems (many people speaking uncivilized languages). Instead, it suggests that the behavior of a few people can be influenced by the environment, but it does not necessarily lead to a chain reaction of more problems. Therefore, option D does not fit the broken window effect as described.\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.\n</think>\n<answer>\nD\n</answer>",
