sion**:\n   - Based on the analysis, Option C is the most accurate description of Gamba's strategy of argumentation. Gamba is refuting Munoz's argument by showing that the 15 opposing votes do not guarantee the conclusion that the entire city opposes the new water system.\n\nThe correct option is:<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>C<\uff5cUser\uff5c>Thank you for the detailed explanation. I understand now that the correct option is C. Gamba's strategy is to refute Munoz's argument by showing that the sample size of 15 opposing votes is too small to represent the majority view of Hopeville's residents.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're welcome! Yes, you've understood it correctly. Gamba's strategy is to refute Munoz's argument by pointing out that the sample size of 15 opposing votes is too small to represent the majority view of Hopeville's residents. This directly addresses the issue of the sample size being too small to be representative, which is the core of Gamba's argument. The correct option is indeed C. If you have any more questions or need further clarification, feel free to ask!<\uff5cUser\uff5c>Thank you for the clear explanation. It really helped me understand the reasoning behind the correct option.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're very welcome! I'm glad I could help clarify the reasoning. If you have any more questions or need further explanations on logical reasoning problems, feel free to ask. I'm here to help!<",
