messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn public speeches, some people talk long and talk endlessly; some people condense their meaning into one sentence, and this sentence is like a heavy stone, stirring up waves in the calm mind of the audience It is commendable and memorable. On October 19, 1936, at the meeting of people from all walks of life in Shanghai to sacrifice Lu Xun, my country\'s famous journalist, politician, and social activist Mr. Zou Taofen delivered a speech of only 33 words: Not too soon, I would like to commemorate Mr. with one sentence: Many people have fallen without a fight, and Mr. Lu Xun has fallen without a fight.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is the main expression of this text?\n# Options:\nA) Short speeches, such as zou taofen\'s one-sentence speech, have profound meaning and strong expressive effects\nB) The phrase unyielding in battle accurately outlines mr. lu xun\'s fighting spirit\nC) The word war contains how much people admire and praise mr. lu xun\nD) Many shameless literati not only do not fight, but also slave their hands and knees; but the gentleman\'s eyebrows are cold and stubbornI think the correct option is: D\n\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and the question step by step:\n1. The context provides an example of a memorable speech by Zou Taofen, which was only 33 words long. This speech was delivered at a memorial event for Lu Xun.\n2. The question asks us to identify the main expression of the text based on the given information.\n3. We need to analyze each option carefully to determine which one best captures the essence of the text.\nOption A: "Short speeches, such as Zou Taofen\'s one-sentence speech, have profound meaning and strong expressive effects"\n- This option aligns well with the context. The text mentions that Zou Taofen\'s speech was short and impactful, which is consistent with the idea that short speeches can have profound meaning and strong expressive effects.\nOption B: "The phrase \'unyielding in battle\' accurately outlines Mr. Lu Xun\'s fighting spirit"\n- While this option touches on Lu Xun\'s fighting spirit, it doesn\'t capture the main expression of the text. The text is more focused on Zou Taofen\'s speech and its impact rather than directly discussing Lu Xun\'s fighting spirit.\nOption C: "The word \'war\' contains how much people admire and praise Mr. Lu Xun"\n- This option seems to misinterpret the text. The word "war" is not mentioned in the context, and the text doesn\'t focus on people\'s admiration for Lu Xun.\nOption D: "Many shameless literati not only do not fight, but also slave their hands and knees; but the gentleman\'s eyebrows are cold and stubborn"\n- This option appears to be a misquote or unrelated statement from the text. It doesn\'t align with the context provided.\nAfter analyzing each option, the one that best captures the main expression of the text is Option A.\n</think>\n<answer>\nA\n</answer>\nThe correct option is:']
