messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn most cases, writing poems and filling words is a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion. It is unpredictable for a beginner to have what kind of feelings and choose what kind of sentence pattern to start with. But once he has a preliminary idea, he can always get appropriate help in the book Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms. He will know which words are suitable to express what kind of feelings, what kind of rhyme he should choose, and how to make rational use of certain rhetorical devices so as not to be fooled in the face of special syntax. If you have read enough ancient poems and have a certain sense of language, you will indeed be able to complete your first creation with the help of this book. It can not teach people to write amazing masterpieces, but with the greatest sincerity to prevent you from making all kinds of jokes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings is the main content of this text?\n# Options:\nA) Tang and song poetry rhythms is suitable for beginners because of its rich tones\nB) Poetry creation is essentially a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion\nC) Tang and song poetry rhythms provides a very good help for beginners\nD) The creator of poetry must have abundant emotion and high literary accomplishmentI think the correct option is: D\n\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, I need to carefully analyze the context and question to determine the main content of the text. Let\'s break it down step by step:\n\n1. **Context Analysis**:\n   - The text discusses the process of writing poems and the role of Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms.\n   - It mentions that beginners may struggle with choosing appropriate feelings and sentence patterns.\n   - The book provides guidance on suitable words, rhyme, and rhetorical devices.\n   - It emphasizes that while the book cannot teach amazing masterpieces, it can prevent beginners from making "all kinds of jokes."\n\n2. **Question Analysis**:\n   - The question asks for the main content of the text based on the given information.\n\n3. **Option Analysis**:\n   - **Option A**: "Tang and song poetry rhythms is suitable for beginners because of its rich tones"\n     - The text does mention the book provides guidance on suitable words and rhyme, but it does not specifically highlight "rich tones" as the main reason.\n   - **Option B**: "Poetry creation is essentially a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion"\n     - While the text does mention that writing poems involves mutual accommodation, this is not the main focus of the text.\n   - **Option C**: "Tang and song poetry rhythms provides a very good help for beginners"\n     - This option aligns well with the text\'s emphasis on the book\'s role in providing guidance and preventing beginners from making mistakes.\n   - **Option D**: "The creator of poetry must have abundant emotion and high literary accomplishment"\n     - The text does not discuss the emotional or literary accomplishments of the creator, but rather focuses on the process of writing and the book\'s role.\nThe correct option is:']
