      "text": "B<\uff5cUser\uff5c>I think the correct option is B. Let me explain why:\n\n- The context states that depositors benefit from the insurance provided by the government.\n- The argument concludes that since depositors benefit, they should bear the cost of the insurance.\n- Option B directly supports this conclusion by stating that those who benefit from a service should bear the costs of that service.\n- Option A is about the structure of insurance premiums and does not address the burden of cost on depositors.\n- Option C is about the availability of services and does not relate to the cost-sharing aspect.\n- Option D is about the conditions under which government-backed security should be provided and does not address the burden of cost on depositors.\n\nTherefore, the principle that most justifies the conclusion of the argument is Option B. <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You are correct. The principle that most justifies the conclusion of the argument is Option B: \"The people who stand to benefit from an economic service should always be made to bear the costs of that service.\" This principle directly aligns with the argument's reasoning that since depositors benefit from the insurance, they should bear the cost of it. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Thank you for the detailed explanation. I now understand why option B is the correct answer.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're welcome! If you have any more questions or need further clarification, feel free to ask. Understanding logical reasoning problems can be quite helpful in various contexts. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Absolutely, understanding these principles will definitely help in solving similar problems in the future. Thank you for your help!\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're very welcome! If you have any more questions or need further assistance, don't hesitate to ask. Good luck with your studies and problem-solving! <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Thank you, I will. Have a great day!\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You too! If you need more help, w