messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe term boundary problem refers to various short-sighted behaviors of employees due to the short employment relationship in modern enterprises, and the harm caused by such behaviors to the enterprise\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings belongs to the term boundary problem\n# Options:\nA) Because he will retire in one year, lao zhao feels unable and his work efficiency is getting worse and worse\nB) Because he was not familiar with the business, xiao li, who had just come a month, lost a big customer and the company lost a lot\nC) Because he felt that it was impossible to become a regular worker,xiao wang worked hard every day to show himself \nD) Because he only signed a contract for half a year, xiao sun ignored the use of working machinery and equipmentI think the correct option is: B\n\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and the question step by step:\n\n1. **Understanding the Context:**\n   - The term "boundary problem" refers to short-sighted behaviors of employees due to the short-term nature of their employment in modern enterprises.\n   - These behaviors can cause harm to the enterprise.\n\n2. **Analyzing the Question:**\n   - We need to identify which of the given options represents a short-sighted behavior due to the short-term nature of employment.\n\n3. **Option Analysis:**\n   - **Option A:** "Because he will retire in one year, lao zhao feels unable and his work efficiency is getting worse and worse."\n     - This option suggests that lao zhao\'s work efficiency is declining because he feels he has a limited time left in the job. This could be a short-sighted behavior due to the short-term nature of his employment.\n   - **Option B:** "Because he was not familiar with the business, xiao li, who had just come a month, lost a big customer and the company lost a lot."\n     - This option describes a situation where xiao li\'s unfamiliarity with the business led to a loss. This is more about inexperience rather than short-term employment.\n   - **Option C:** "Because he felt that it was impossible to become a regular worker, xiao wang worked hard every day to show himself."\n     - This option suggests that xiao wang is working hard to impress the employer, which could be a proactive behavior rather than a short-sighted one due to the short-term nature of his employment.\n   - **Option D:** "Because he only signed a contract for half a year, xiao sun ignored the use of working machinery and equipment."\n     - This option indicates that xiao sun disregarded proper use of machinery due to the short-term contract. This could be a short-sighted behavior due to the short-term nature of his employment.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - Both options A and D describe short-sighted behaviors due to the short-term nature of employment. However, option A is more directly related to the context of the term boundary problem as it explicitly mentions the short-term nature of the employment leading to a decline in work efficiency.\n   - Option B and C do not fit the context as well as they describe inexperience and proactive behavior respectively.\nThe correct option is:']
