messages:  ["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nShell oil company ranks first in the total net profit of 500 major companies in the world for three consecutive years, mainly because it has a lot of international business.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, best supports the above statement?\n# Options:\nA) The profits of oil companies with the same scale as shell but less international business are lower than shell.\nB) In history, the champion of the net profit of the world's 500 major companies is oil companies.\nC) Over the past three years, the world's 500 largest companies have been trying to move towards internationalization.\nD) In the past three years, the prices of oil and refined oil have been very stable.I think the correct option is: B\n\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the context and the question step by step. The context provides us with the following information:\n- Shell oil company ranks first in the total net profit of 500 major companies in the world for three consecutive years.\n- The reason given for this ranking is that Shell has a lot of international business.\n\nThe question asks us to identify which option best supports the statement that Shell's success is due to its extensive international business. We need to evaluate each option to see which one provides the strongest evidence for this claim.\n\nLet's analyze each option:\n\nA) The profits of oil companies with the same scale as Shell but less international business are lower than Shell.\n- This option directly compares Shell's performance with other oil companies of similar scale but with less international business. If these companies have lower profits, it strongly supports the idea that Shell's international business is a key factor in its success.\n\nB) In history, the champion of the net profit of the world's 500 major companies is oil companies.\n- This statement is about the historical trend of oil companies being champions, but it does not provide any specific information about Shell's international business or its impact on its profits.\n\nC) Over the past three years, the world's 500 largest companies have been trying to move towards internationalization.\n- While this statement indicates a trend in the industry, it does not directly support the claim that Shell's international business is the reason for its success. It merely suggests that many companies are becoming more international, but it doesn't provide evidence specific to Shell.\n\nD) In the past three years, the prices of oil and refined oil have been very stable.\n- This option talks about the stability of oil prices, which is not directly related to Shell's international business. Stable oil prices could be a factor, but they do not specifically support the claim that international business is the reason for Shell's success.\nThe correct option is:"]
