onclusion is true, it leads to a contradiction.\n   - **Option B: Establishing that experience teaches us the opposite of what lance concludes**\n     - Frank does not argue that experience teaches the opposite. He is not addressing the nature of experience but rather the logical implications of Lance\'s conclusion.\n   - **Option C: Showing that lance\'s conclusion involves him in a contradiction**\n     - Frank\'s argument does involve a contradiction. If Lance\'s conclusion is true, then there must be a general rule with no exceptions, which contradicts Lance\'s own statement that every general rule has at least one exception.\n   - **Option D: Showing that it has no implications for any real cases**\n     - Frank\'s argument does have implications for real cases. It shows that if Lance\'s conclusion is true, it leads to a specific contradiction.\nThe correct option is:']
