  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "B) The most diligent people in the world may not be able to read all the books in the world.\nLet's analyze why the other options are incorrect:\nA) The most diligent person in the world cannot read all the books in the world.\n- This option is too specific. The context only states that the most diligent people cannot read all the books, not that the most diligent person cannot.\nC) The most diligent person in the world may read all the books in the world.\n- This option contradicts the given context. The context clearly states that even the most diligent people cannot read all the books.\nD) People who read all the books in the world must be the most diligent people in the world.\n- This option is also incorrect. The context does not provide any information about people who read all the books being the most diligent.\nTherefore, the correct option is B.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB\n</answer>",
