_2 \\) (since the speeds are the same).\n   - This implies \\( t_1 = t_2 \\).\n\n4. **Comparison of Times:**\n   - A takes time \\( t_1 \\) to walk \\( \\frac{D}{2} \\) and \\( t_2 \\) to run \\( \\frac{D}{2} \\).\n   - B takes \\( t_1 \\) to walk and \\( t_1 \\) to run.\n   - Since \\( t_1 = t_2 \\) and \\( t_1 = t_1 \\), the total time taken by B is \\( t_1 + t_1 = 2t_1 \\).\n   - The total time taken by A is \\( t_1 + t_2 = t_1 + t_1 = 2t_1 \\).\n\n5. **Conclusion:**\n   - Both A and B take the same total time to reach the classroom.\nThe correct option is:"]
