ignal type that could potentially be detected.\n- Option B: This option states that most people who have survived after being trapped in collapsed buildings were rescued within two hours of the building's collapse. This information is about the effectiveness of rescue operations and does not directly relate to the performance of the new sensing device. It does not strengthen the argument about the device's ability to locate trapped individuals.\n- Option C: This option mentions that extensive training is required to operate the device effectively. While this might be a concern for emergency teams, it does not directly support the claim that the device will improve their ability to locate trapped individuals. It introduces a potential barrier to using the device.\n- Option D: This option states that the device gives a distinctive reading when the signals it detects come from human beings rather than from any other living beings. This is the most relevant option because it directly supports the claim that the device can accurately detect and locate human beings, which is the primary purpose of the device. If the device can distinguish between human signals and other signals, it would significantly enhance the emergency teams' ability to locate trapped individuals.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe correct option is:"]
