point of the argument by suggesting that the harmful radiolytic products are rare or not commonly found.\n2. Option B: "Cancer and other serious health problems have many causes that are unrelated to radioactive substances and gamma rays."\n   - This option weakens the third point by suggesting that the health problems are not directly caused by the irradiation process.\n3. Option C: "A study showed that irradiation leaves the vitamin content of virtually all fruits and vegetables unchanged."\n   - This option weakens the second point of the argument by providing evidence that irradiation does not reduce the vitamin content.\n4. Option D: "A study showed that the cancer rate is no higher among people who eat irradiated food than among those who do not."\n   - This option weakens the third point by providing evidence that there is no increased cancer risk associated with eating irradiated foods.\nThe correct option is:']
