messages:  ["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nDetective: Because the embezzler must have had specialized knowledge and access to internal financial records, we can presume that the embezzler worked for XYZ Corporation as either an accountant or an actuary. But an accountant would probably not make the kind of mistakes in ledger entries that led to the discovery of the embezzlement. Thus it is likely that the embezzler is one of the actuaries.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, each of the following weakens the detective's argument EXCEPT:\n# Options:\nA) An independent report released before the crime took place concluded that xyz corporation was vulnerable to embezzlement.\nB) There is evidence of breaches in computer security at the time of the embezzlement that could have given persons outside xyz corporation access to internal financial records.\nC) The actuaries' activities while working for xyz corporation were more closely scrutinized by supervisors than were the activities of the accountants.\nD) Xyz corporation employs eight accountants, whereas it has only two actuaries on its staff.I think the correct option is: D\n\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the detective's argument and analyze each option to determine which one does not weaken the argument. The detective's argument can be summarized as follows:\n\n1. The embezzler must have had specialized knowledge and access to internal financial records.\n2. The embezzler likely worked for XYZ Corporation as either an accountant or an actuary.\n3. An accountant would not make the kind of mistakes that led to the discovery of the embezzlement.\n4. Therefore, it is likely that the embezzler is one of the actuaries.\n\nNow, let's examine each option to see if it weakens or supports the detective's argument:\n\nA) An independent report released before the crime took place concluded that XYZ Corporation was vulnerable to embezzlement.\n- This option suggests that the company was already known to be vulnerable, which could imply that the embezzler might have been someone other than an actuary. This weakens the detective's argument.\n\nB) There is evidence of breaches in computer security at the time of the embezzlement that could have given persons outside XYZ Corporation access to internal financial records.\n- This option introduces an alternative source of access to internal financial records, which could mean that the embezzler might not have been an actuary. This weakens the detective's argument.\n\nC) The actuaries' activities while working for XYZ Corporation were more closely scrutinized by supervisors than were the activities of the accountants.\n- This option suggests that the actuaries' activities were more closely monitored, which could imply that they were less likely to make the kind of mistakes that led to the discovery of the embezzlement. This weakens the detective's argument.\n\nD) XYZ Corporation employs eight accountants, whereas it has only two actuaries on its staff.\n- This option provides information about the staffing levels but does not directly address the likelihood of the embezzler being an actuary. It neither weakens nor strengthens the detective's argument.\nThe correct option is:"]
