rrect game receipt:**\n   - Liam (basketball)\n   - Noah (soccer)\n   - Oliver (basketball)\n\nThis solution satisfies the condition that each guess is half right:\n- Guess by Liam: Noah (soccer) is incorrect, Oliver (basketball) is correct.\n- Guess by Noah: Liam (basketball) is correct, Oliver (chess) is incorrect.\n- Guess by Oliver: Liam (chess) is incorrect, Noah (soccer) is correct.\n\nThe correct option is: B) Liam received a basketball, Noah received a chess, and Oliver received a soccer.\n\n### Problem 2:\n# Context:\nThree friends, Mia, Peter, and Quinn, made guesses about which of three different types of movies (action, comedy, or drama) each of them received. Their guesses were as follows:\n- Mia guessed: Peter received an action and Quinn received a comedy.\n- Peter guessed: Mia received a comedy and Quinn received a drama.\n- Quinn guessed: Mia received a drama and Peter received an action.\n\nIt is known that exactly one of their guesses was correct for each person.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is their correct movie receipt?\n# Options:\nA) Mia received an action, Peter received a comedy, and Quinn received a drama.\nB) Mia received a comedy, Peter received a drama, and Quinn received an action.\nC) Mia received a drama, Peter received an action, and Quinn received a comedy.\nD) Mia received a drama, Peter received an action, and Quinn received a comedy.\n\n**Solution:**\n1. **Identify the guesses:**\n   - Mia: Peter (action), Quinn (comedy)\n   - Peter: Mia (comedy), Quinn (drama)\n   - Quinn: Mia (drama), Peter (action)\n\n2. **Analyze each guess:**\n   - **Guess by Mia:**\n     - Peter (action) is incorrect.\n     - Quinn (comedy) is correct.\n     - This means Peter did not receive an action and Quinn received a comedy.\n   \n   - **Guess by Peter:**\n     - Mia (comedy) is correct.\n     - Quinn (drama) is incorrect.\n     - This means Mia received a comedy and Quinn did not receive a drama.\n   \n   - **Guess by Quinn:**\n     - Mia (drama) is incorrect.\n     - Peter (action) is correct.\n     - This means Mia did not receive a drama and Peter received an action.\n\n3. **Combine the information:**\n   - From Guess by Mia: Quinn (comedy)\n   - From Guess by Peter: Mia (comedy)\n   - From Guess by Quinn: Peter (action)\n\n4. **Determine the correct movie receipt:**\n   - Mia (comedy)\n   - Peter (action)\n   - Quinn (comedy)\n\nThis solution satisfies the condition that each guess is half right:\n- Guess by Mia: Peter (action) is incorrect, Quinn (comedy) is correct.\n- Guess by Peter: Mia (comedy) is correct, Quinn (drama) is incorrect.\n- Guess by Quinn: Mia (drama) is incorrect, Peter (action) is correct.\n\nThe correct option is: B) Mia received a comedy, Peter received a drama, and Quinn received an action.\n\n### Problem 3:\n# Context:\nThree friends, Sam, Taylor, and Uma, made guesses about which of three different types of snacks (chips, cookies, or pretzels) each of them received. Their guesses were as follows:\n- Sam guessed: Taylor received a chips and Uma received a cookies.\n- Taylor guessed: Sam received a cookies and Uma received a pretzels.\n- Uma guessed: Sam received a pretzels and Taylor received a chips.\n\nIt is known that exactly one of their guesses was correct for each person.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is their correct snack receipt?\n# Options:\nA) Sam received a chips, Taylor received a cookies, and Uma received a pretzels.\nB) Sam received a cookies, Taylor received a pretzels, and Uma received a chips.\nC) Sam received a pretzels, Taylor received a chips, and Uma received a cookies.\nD) Sam received a pretzels, Taylor received a cookies, and Uma received a chips.\n\n**Solution:**\n1. **Identify the guesses:**\n   - Sam: Taylor (chips), Uma (cookies)\n   - Taylor: Sam (cookies), Uma (pretzels)\n   - Uma: Sam (pretzels), Taylor (chips)\n\n2. **Analyze each guess:**\n   - **Guess