e, Emily received a truck, and Frank received a car.\n\n**Solution:**\n1. **Identify the guesses:**\n   - David: Emily (car), Frank (truck)\n   - Emily: David (truck), Frank (motorcycle)\n   - Frank: David (motorcycle), Emily (car)\n\n2. **Analyze each guess:**\n   - **Guess by David:**\n     - Emily (car) is incorrect.\n     - Frank (truck) is correct.\n     - This means Emily did not receive a car and Frank received a truck.\n   \n   - **Guess by Emily:**\n     - David (truck) is correct.\n     - Frank (motorcycle) is incorrect.\n     - This means David received a truck and Frank did not receive a motorcycle.\n   \n   - **Guess by Frank:**\n     - David (motorcycle) is incorrect.\n     - Emily (car) is correct.\n     - This means David did not receive a motorcycle and Emily received a car.\n\n3. **Combine the information:**\n   - From Guess by David: Frank (truck)\n   - From Guess by Emily: David (truck)\n   - From Guess by Frank: Emily (car)\n\n4. **Determine the correct vehicle receipt:**\n   - David (truck)\n   - Emily (car)\n   - Frank (truck)\n\nThis solution satisfies the condition that each guess is half right:\n- Guess by David: Emily (car) is incorrect, Frank (truck) is correct.\n- Guess by Emily: David (truck) is correct, Frank (motorcycle) is incorrect.\n- Guess by Frank: David (motorcycle) is incorrect, Emily (car) is correct.\n\nThe correct option is: B) David received a truck, Emily received a motorcycle, and Frank received a car.\n\n### Problem 11:\n# Context:\nThree friends, Grace, Henry, and Ivy, made guesses about which of three different types of fruits (apple, banana, or cherry) each of them received. Their guesses were as follows:\n- Grace guessed: Henry received an apple and Ivy received a banana.\n- Henry guessed: Grace received a banana and Ivy received a cherry.\n- Ivy guessed: Grace received a cherry and Henry received an apple.\n\nIt is known that exactly one of their guesses was correct for each person.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the abov