lows:\n- Sam guessed: Tom received a coffee and Uma received a tea.\n- Tom guessed: Sam received a tea and Uma received a juice.\n- Uma guessed: Sam received a juice and Tom received a coffee.\n\nIt is known that exactly one of their guesses was correct for each person.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is their correct drink receipt?\n# Options:\nA) Sam received a coffee, Tom received a tea, and Uma received a juice.\nB) Sam received a tea, Tom received a juice, and Uma received a coffee.\nC) Sam received a juice, Tom received a coffee, and Uma received a tea.\nD) Sam received a juice, Tom received a tea, and Uma received a coffee.\n\n**Solution:**\n1. **Identify the guesses:**\n   - Sam: Tom (coffee), Uma (tea)\n   - Tom: Sam (tea), Uma (juice)\n   - Uma: Sam (juice), Tom (coffee)\n\n2. **Analyze each guess:**\n   - **Guess by Sam:**\n     - Tom (coffee) is incorrect.\n     - Uma (tea) is correct.\n     - This means Tom did not receive a coffee and Uma received a tea.\n   \n   - **Guess by Tom:**\n     - Sam (tea) is correct.\n     - Uma (juice) is incorrect.\n     - This means Sam received a tea and Uma did not receive a juice.\n   \n   - **Guess by Uma:**\n     - Sam (juice) is incorrect.\n     - Tom (coffee) is correct.\n     - This means Sam did not receive a juice and Tom received a coffee.\n\n3. **Combine the information:**\n   - From Guess by Sam: Uma (tea)\n   - From Guess by Tom: Sam (tea)\n   - From Guess by Uma: Tom (coffee)\n\n4. **Determine the correct drink receipt:**\n   - Sam (tea)\n   - Tom (coffee)\n   - Uma (tea)\n\nThis solution satisfies the condition that each guess is half right:\n- Guess by Sam: Tom (coffee) is incorrect, Uma (tea) is correct.\n- Guess by Tom: Sam (tea) is correct, Uma (juice) is incorrect.\n- Guess by Uma: Sam (juice) is incorrect, Tom (coffee) is correct.\n\nThe correct option is: B) Sam received a tea, Tom received a juice, and Uma received a coffee. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Thank yo