 (juice) is incorrect.\n- Guess by Uma: Sam (juice) is incorrect, Tom (coffee) is correct.\n\nThe correct option is: B) Sam received a tea, Tom received a juice, and Uma received a coffee. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Thank you for the detailed solutions to the additional practice problems. They are very helpful. If you have more practice problems or explanations, please share.\n\n<think>\nYou're welcome! I'm glad you found the solutions helpful. Here are a few more practice problems to further enhance your logical reasoning skills:\n\n### Problem 16:\n# Context:\nThree friends, David, Emily, and Frank, made guesses about which of three different types of vehicles (car, truck, or motorcycle) each of them received. Their guesses were as follows:\n- David guessed: Emily received a car and Frank received a truck.\n- Emily guessed: David received a truck and Frank received a motorcycle.\n- Frank guessed: David received a motorcycle and Emily received a car.\n\nIt is known that exactly one of their guesses was correct for each person.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is their correct vehicle receipt?\n# Options:\nA) David received a car, Emily received a truck, and Frank received a motorcycle.\nB) David received a truck, Emily received a motorcycle, and Frank received a car.\nC) David received a motorcycle, Emily received a car, and Frank received a truck.\nD) David received a motorcycle, Emily received a truck, and Frank received a car.\n\n### Problem 17:\n# Context:\nThree friends, Grace, Henry, and Ivy, made guesses about which of three different types of fruits (apple, banana, or cherry) each of them received. Their guesses were as follows:\n- Grace guessed: Henry received an apple and Ivy received a banana.\n- Henry guessed: Grace received a banana and Ivy received a cherry.\n- Ivy guessed: Grace received a cherry and Henry received an apple.\n\nIt is known that exactly one of their guesses was correct for each person.\n\n# Questio