      "text": "D\n\n<answer>\nThe power of traditional culture forced Buddhism to adopt flexible strategies in its dissemination.\nThis option best summarizes the main idea of the passage. The context emphasizes that Buddhism needs to adapt to survive in China, and an example is given of changing the concept of filial piety to align with Chinese culture. This indicates that traditional culture (in this case, Chinese culture) had a significant influence on Buddhism's dissemination strategy.\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.\n</answer>",
