y challenge the belief that lower power consumption will lead to increased sales.\n\nB) The after-sales service quality of this air conditioner is not comparable to other similar products.\n- This option addresses after-sales service quality, which is not mentioned in the context. Even if the after-sales service is poor, it does not directly challenge the belief that lower power consumption will lead to increased sales.\n\nC) The service life of this air conditioner is lower than the average of similar products.\n- This option addresses the service life of the air conditioner. If the service life is shorter, it might reduce customer satisfaction and loyalty, which could negatively impact sales. However, it does not directly challenge the belief that lower power consumption will lead to increased sales.\n\nD) Power consumption is not the main concern of most consumers when choosing air conditioners.\n- This option directly challenges the company's belief. If power consumption is not the main concern for most consumers, then the fact that this air conditioner uses less electricity might not be a significant selling point. This would challenge the company's judgment that lower power consumption will lead to increased sales.\nThe correct option is:"]
