messages:  ["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nWith a record number of new companies starting up in Derderia, and with previously established companies adding many new jobs, a record number of new jobs were created last year in the Derderian economy. This year, previously established companies will not be adding as many new jobs overall as such companies added last year. Ttherefore, unless a record number of companies start up this year, Derderia will not break its record for new jobs created.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is an assumption on which the argument relies?\n# Options:\nA) This year, the new companies starting up will not provide substantially more jobs per company than did new companies last year.\nB) The number of people seeking employment is no larger this year than it was last year.\nC) In a given year, new companies starting up create more new jobs on average than do previously established companies.\nD) The number of jobs created in the derderian economy last year was substantially larger than the number of jobs lost.I think the correct option is: C\n\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the context and the argument step by step. The context provides us with the following information:\n1. Last year, a record number of new companies started up and added many new jobs.\n2. This year, previously established companies will add fewer new jobs overall than they did last year.\n3. The argument concludes that unless a record number of new companies start up this year, Derderia will not break its record for new jobs created.\n\nThe core of the argument is that the number of new companies starting up is crucial for breaking the record for new jobs created. The argument assumes that if the number of new companies does not reach a record level, the total number of new jobs created will not match last year's record.\nThe correct option is:"]
